1
00:00:10,074 --> 00:00:14,178
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:15,647 --> 00:00:17,348
RRRRRAAAARRRRGH!

3
00:00:17,348 --> 00:00:21,386
[incoherent raging]

4
00:00:21,386 --> 00:00:21,986
Wait!

5
00:00:21,986 --> 00:00:23,921
I have satchel charges!

6
00:00:23,921 --> 00:00:25,923
I can bring this whole building down.

7
00:00:25,923 --> 00:00:28,192
Just need to find the right place.

8
00:00:28,192 --> 00:00:29,560
I need to get higher up,

9
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:33,197
then I can find some sort of support
beam to really collapse this place.

10
00:00:33,197 --> 00:00:35,566
I forgot I was even holding these things.

11
00:00:35,566 --> 00:00:39,504
Yeah, now I'm feeling a lot better
about how I'm getting out of here.

12
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:42,306
It's no longer an "if" situation.

13
00:00:42,306 --> 00:00:45,576
Honestly, this amount of
ordnance is a real comfort factor.

14
00:00:45,576 --> 00:00:48,479
It's like having a square
explosive teddy bear.

15
00:00:48,479 --> 00:00:51,416
I need a marker so I can put a
little smiley face on it.

16
00:00:51,416 --> 00:00:52,417
Give it a name.

17
00:00:52,417 --> 00:00:55,486
Now, the most obvious ones are
"Boomer" or "Boo-boo".

18
00:00:55,486 --> 00:00:59,490
But if I named it something like "Chuck",
that has some nice subtleties to it.

19
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:02,060
Hm, I'm not seeing any
obvious spots here.

20
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,861
It would be better if I could
place the charges

21
00:01:03,861 --> 00:01:06,230
closer to where I could see
daylight at least.

22
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:09,767
Actually, I could get passed
this conveyor.

23
00:01:09,767 --> 00:01:12,670
I'll try that first, then I'll
blow up the building.

24
00:01:13,905 --> 00:01:15,673
Hah.  Guard rails.

25
00:01:15,673 --> 00:01:17,075
Yeah, safety first!

26
00:01:17,975 --> 00:01:18,609
...'kay...

27
00:01:19,510 --> 00:01:21,079
This isn't so bad...

28
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:24,182
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
"Radioactive"?!

29
00:01:24,182 --> 00:01:26,084
Are we saying crushing, drowning,

30
00:01:26,084 --> 00:01:29,821
burning, exploding isn't
thorough enough for this place?

31
00:01:29,821 --> 00:01:34,992
Eh, screw it.  I have a Geiger counter
in my suit because I am trendy.

32
00:01:34,992 --> 00:01:36,894
I'm a fashion pioneer.

33
00:01:36,894 --> 00:01:40,565
So, I'll decide for myself if
this place is radioactive or not.

34
00:01:40,565 --> 00:01:43,267
For all I know, they could be
talking about the sun.

35
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:45,103
It can be seen from a window.

36
00:01:45,103 --> 00:01:46,104
"Warning!"

37
00:01:46,104 --> 00:01:46,738
DROP-OFF!

38
00:01:47,638 --> 00:01:48,072
Ugh!

39
00:01:48,539 --> 00:01:51,476
Are you kidding?  This is even
worse than I expected!

40
00:01:51,476 --> 00:01:54,011
This is something out of cartoon!

41
00:01:54,011 --> 00:01:55,713
Oh my God!

42
00:01:55,713 --> 00:01:58,850
Those jaws killed space bug
like an Earth bug!

43
00:01:58,850 --> 00:01:59,917
Oh, wow!

44
00:01:59,917 --> 00:02:01,385
My lucky day!

45
00:02:01,385 --> 00:02:03,121
This is a dream come true!

46
00:02:03,121 --> 00:02:06,023
I was a kid and I went to
see Santa Claus,

47
00:02:06,023 --> 00:02:07,558
I told him I wanted to be in a cage fight

48
00:02:07,558 --> 00:02:10,228
with these tiny fucking monsters
jumping at my face.

49
00:02:10,228 --> 00:02:12,330
And I wanted the floor to be
made of a giant crusher

50
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:14,398
that could kill me in one quick motion

51
00:02:14,398 --> 00:02:18,102
AND THE SIDES TO BE SLANTED,
SO IF I SLIPPED, I'D IMMEDIATELY DIE!

52
00:02:18,102 --> 00:02:19,504
AND NOW I HAVE IT ALL!

53
00:02:19,504 --> 00:02:21,873
WHAT MORE COULD I POSSIBLY ASK FOR?!

54
00:02:21,873 --> 00:02:24,876
Christ, I hate having to make
decisions under pressure like this.

55
00:02:24,876 --> 00:02:26,978
Of course, there's only one option, so...

56
00:02:27,879 --> 00:02:30,948
Oh-ho... Jell-O knees...

57
00:02:30,948 --> 00:02:32,750
I feel sore...

58
00:02:33,317 --> 00:02:37,688
I think I'll take a dip in this
thoughtfully provided bath of...

59
00:02:37,688 --> 00:02:40,258
green glowing liquid that's...

60
00:02:41,125 --> 00:02:43,895
Oh, wait, this is a trap.

61
00:02:43,895 --> 00:02:46,430
I'm not falling for that.

62
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:48,332
This isn't even a spa.

63
00:02:48,332 --> 00:02:49,600
What the fuck?

64
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,602
It's like they're not even trying.

65
00:02:51,602 --> 00:02:53,070
Oh, yeah, "Radiation".

66
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:54,438
Woo-oo-oo...

67
00:02:54,438 --> 00:02:58,876
Well, my Geiger counter still hasn't
gone off, so, you're a liar, Mr. Sign.

68
00:02:58,876 --> 00:03:00,545
You'll fit right in this place.

69
00:03:00,545 --> 00:03:03,881
What is it with this intense red
lighting and cramped corridors?

70
00:03:03,881 --> 00:03:05,349
I feel like I'm on a sub.

71
00:03:05,349 --> 00:03:07,552
This designer must've been Navy.

72
00:03:07,552 --> 00:03:09,554
Oh, damn.  A grate over top.

73
00:03:09,554 --> 00:03:10,988
Is this necessary?

74
00:03:10,988 --> 00:03:11,789
If there's someone up there,

75
00:03:11,789 --> 00:03:15,092
I'm going to pop up and say I'm
a troll and want some goat meat.

76
00:03:15,092 --> 00:03:18,262
Oh, God, they locked this, too?

77
00:03:18,262 --> 00:03:21,098
All right, well, I don't have
much else to work on.

78
00:03:21,098 --> 00:03:21,933
Oh, that opened right up.

79
00:03:21,933 --> 00:03:23,901
[houndeyes charging up]
Oh, that opened right up.

80
00:03:23,901 --> 00:03:25,369
[houndeyes charging up]
Okay, I'm your dance instructor--

81
00:03:25,369 --> 00:03:26,771
NO, YOU'RE STARTING TOO EARLY!

82
00:03:26,771 --> 00:03:27,572
STOP THAT!

83
00:03:27,572 --> 00:03:28,773
I SAID STOP THAT!

84
00:03:28,773 --> 00:03:29,841
1-2-3 LEFT!

85
00:03:30,107 --> 00:03:31,175
1-2-3 LEFT!

86
00:03:31,475 --> 00:03:33,744
NO, NO, YOUR RHYTHM'S ALL WRONG!

87
00:03:33,744 --> 00:03:34,679
Rrrgh!

88
00:03:34,679 --> 00:03:37,114
I give up; I can't teach this class.

89
00:03:37,114 --> 00:03:39,684
Some people just don't
want to learn, y'know?

90
00:03:40,284 --> 00:03:42,320
Oh, hey, there's a box of ammo.

91
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,422
Hell, these will fit the revolver.

92
00:03:44,422 --> 00:03:47,058
I guess being a teacher
does have its perks.

93
00:03:47,058 --> 00:03:49,327
Oh, nice, it comes with a speed-loader.

94
00:03:49,327 --> 00:03:51,863
Though, I guess if you need a speed-loader,

95
00:03:51,863 --> 00:03:54,599
you shouldn't be using a
revolver in the first place.

96
00:03:54,599 --> 00:03:56,601
But, here I am.

97
00:03:56,601 --> 00:04:00,137
In some sort of dog kennel...I guess.

98
00:04:00,137 --> 00:04:03,040
Except I'm on the wrong side of it.

99
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:05,610
I'm getting out--no, maybe not.

100
00:04:05,610 --> 00:04:09,981
It's the amps that kill you, but
do I really want the volts either?

101
00:04:09,981 --> 00:04:13,517
Well, the people who built this
kennel didn't count on one thing:

102
00:04:13,517 --> 00:04:15,987
I'm not a dog!

103
00:04:15,987 --> 00:04:19,991
Actually, if the fence wasn't electrified,
I think a dog could get out of here.

104
00:04:19,991 --> 00:04:24,161
But, I'm part of the Opposable Thumbs
Club, so I think I'll play it safe.

105
00:04:24,161 --> 00:04:25,363
Oh, yeah, this'll hold me.

106
00:04:27,632 --> 00:04:31,469
Now, the trick here is to NOT do
a belly-flop onto the fence.

107
00:04:31,469 --> 00:04:33,471
That would be worst possible outcome.

108
00:04:34,272 --> 00:04:35,273
Oof!

109
00:04:35,273 --> 00:04:36,707
Oh, boy.

110
00:04:36,707 --> 00:04:40,077
Nothing like the loving embrace
of poured concrete.

111
00:04:40,077 --> 00:04:42,813
Y'know, I'm almost disappointed
I DON'T see anyone following me

112
00:04:42,813 --> 00:04:45,650
because I'd like to see them go
through everything I have.

113
00:04:45,650 --> 00:04:47,184
Or, maybe somebody was following me

114
00:04:47,184 --> 00:04:49,921
but they're dead now because
they tried to keep up.

115
00:04:49,921 --> 00:04:52,023
That would be kind of
flattering in a way.

116
00:04:52,023 --> 00:04:53,090
I'm just that good.

117
00:04:53,090 --> 00:04:54,292
[thumping sound]
What?

118
00:04:54,292 --> 00:04:57,128
WHOA!  How did something THAT
big sneak up on me?

119
00:04:57,828 --> 00:04:58,663
Yeah.

120
00:04:58,663 --> 00:05:00,665
Yeah, that got you to calm down.

121
00:05:00,665 --> 00:05:02,934
I can see you know what this is.

122
00:05:02,934 --> 00:05:03,768
Good.

123
00:05:03,768 --> 00:05:06,671
We're having some
interspecies communication.

124
00:05:06,671 --> 00:05:09,073
Damn, you're as big as a linebacker.

125
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,842
Looks like you have some sort of armor...

126
00:05:11,842 --> 00:05:13,411
An extra appendage...

127
00:05:13,411 --> 00:05:17,114
Yeah, you're definitely more impressive
than the rest of the losers here.

128
00:05:17,114 --> 00:05:19,317
I could see you getting
a job in management.

129
00:05:19,317 --> 00:05:21,585
Well, I'll let somebody else dissect you.

130
00:05:21,585 --> 00:05:25,089
I've already done more than my
share in the name of science today.

131
00:05:26,490 --> 00:05:27,158
[lock jiggles]

132
00:05:27,158 --> 00:05:29,226
What is wrong with this world?

133
00:05:29,226 --> 00:05:31,862
All right, where are the keys?
Do you have them?

134
00:05:31,862 --> 00:05:33,431
No, probably not.

135
00:05:34,598 --> 00:05:35,599
Button's locked...

136
00:05:36,667 --> 00:05:38,436
Computer's locked...

137
00:05:38,436 --> 00:05:39,770
Well, I'm the locksmith!

138
00:05:39,770 --> 00:05:41,238
[alarm sounds]
Alarms?

139
00:05:41,238 --> 00:05:42,039
[crashing sound]
You'd think I would--

140
00:05:42,039 --> 00:05:42,873
OH GOD!

141
00:05:42,873 --> 00:05:45,076
SEE, THIS IS WHY PEOPLE NEED TO
DO THEIR OWN WORK!

142
00:05:45,076 --> 00:05:47,611
WHEN I HAVE TO DO THEIR JOBS FOR
THEM, THIS IS WHAT HAPPENS!

143
00:05:48,512 --> 00:05:49,513
Did I kill it?

144
00:05:49,513 --> 00:05:50,281
WAAAH!

145
00:05:50,781 --> 00:05:53,317
Okay, the bullet test is
inconclusive, so...

146
00:05:53,317 --> 00:05:55,853
Let's see how it responds to a
different set of stimuli.

147
00:05:56,787 --> 00:05:59,457
HYPOTHESIS CONFIRMED!

148
00:05:59,457 --> 00:06:00,524
Christ.

149
00:06:00,524 --> 00:06:02,526
I hate biolabs.

150
00:06:02,526 --> 00:06:03,361
Hey, what's this?

151
00:06:03,361 --> 00:06:04,362
[alarm sounds]

152
00:06:04,362 --> 00:06:06,364
[alarm sounds]
Why did a new set of alarms start?

153
00:06:06,364 --> 00:06:07,798
[alarm sounds]

154
00:06:07,798 --> 00:06:09,367
I don't like this.  I'm leaving.

155
00:06:09,367 --> 00:06:10,534
[lock jiggles]

156
00:06:10,534 --> 00:06:11,902
Why is this door locked?

157
00:06:11,902 --> 00:06:13,237
I didn't even shut this.

158
00:06:13,237 --> 00:06:15,072
[machine powers up]

159
00:06:15,072 --> 00:06:15,539
[machine powers up]
Shit.

160
00:06:15,539 --> 00:06:16,741
[machine powers up]

161
00:06:16,741 --> 00:06:19,377
[machine powers up]
I think this what being an atom feels like.

162
00:06:19,377 --> 00:06:21,579
[electrical explosion]

163
00:06:21,579 --> 00:06:22,079
Oh.

164
00:06:22,813 --> 00:06:23,981
Uh.

165
00:06:23,981 --> 00:06:26,584
Well, I feel okay.

166
00:06:26,584 --> 00:06:30,721
But, something tells me
I might sterile now.

167
00:06:30,721 --> 00:06:32,556
Oh, hey!  I need some help!

168
00:06:32,556 --> 00:06:33,391
Don't be shy!

169
00:06:33,391 --> 00:06:34,291
BLAAAH!

170
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:35,426
[babbling]

171
00:06:37,395 --> 00:06:39,663
Wow.  That is BEYOND rude.

172
00:06:39,663 --> 00:06:41,032
Oh, shit!

173
00:06:41,032 --> 00:06:42,099
I forgot.

174
00:06:42,099 --> 00:06:44,101
Everyone's trying to kill me.

175
00:06:44,101 --> 00:06:45,936
Yeah.
OF COURSE!

176
00:06:45,936 --> 00:06:47,938
IT'S NOT MY IMAGINATION!

177
00:06:47,938 --> 00:06:51,042
EVERYONE IS TRYING TO KILL ME!

178
00:06:51,042 --> 00:06:51,942
GUARD: Hey, it's no good--
AH HAH!

179
00:06:53,310 --> 00:06:55,479
FOOL ME ONCE, SHAME ON YOU!

180
00:06:55,479 --> 00:06:58,215
FOOL ME TWICE, EVERYONE DIES!

181
00:06:58,215 --> 00:07:00,217
Yeah, I see right through you.

182
00:07:00,217 --> 00:07:02,787
Standing there, acting like
you're my best friend

183
00:07:02,787 --> 00:07:06,590
when you obviously waved that
assassin right on passed you.

184
00:07:06,590 --> 00:07:08,426
I can't trust anyone here.

185
00:07:08,426 --> 00:07:11,595
But, I never did anyway
so I guess there's no problem!

186
00:07:11,595 --> 00:07:12,463
Yoo-hoo!

187
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:18,102
Over here!
You forgot your bullets!

188
00:07:19,804 --> 00:07:20,738
Take some of mine!

189
00:07:23,908 --> 00:07:25,443
You're welcome!

190
00:07:25,443 --> 00:07:29,246
Hm, I'm going to need some more ammo
if I'm going to kill the whole world.

191
00:07:29,246 --> 00:07:31,782
Oh, here's some guns; that's a start.

192
00:07:31,782 --> 00:07:33,017
I'm a gun farmer.

193
00:07:33,717 --> 00:07:37,088
I plant bullet seeds in people
at about a thousand feet per second and

194
00:07:37,088 --> 00:07:38,889
out pop more guns.

195
00:07:38,889 --> 00:07:40,458
Right now, I'm harvesting.

196
00:07:41,025 --> 00:07:42,259
So.

197
00:07:42,259 --> 00:07:45,796
I admit I really dropped the ball
forgetting everyone was trying to kill me.

198
00:07:45,796 --> 00:07:46,931
That's so unlike me.

199
00:07:46,931 --> 00:07:50,367
Usually, that's the first conclusion
I come to when things go wrong.

200
00:07:50,367 --> 00:07:53,471
If anything, it's less stressful
now since I don't have to wonder

201
00:07:53,471 --> 00:07:54,738
if they're going to kill me.

202
00:07:54,738 --> 00:07:56,440
I know they are.

203
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,641
Oh.  Ammo.

204
00:07:57,641 --> 00:08:00,444
No more second-guessing people
when they give me shifty looks

205
00:08:00,444 --> 00:08:03,013
around the coffee machine or
pass me in the hall.

206
00:08:03,013 --> 00:08:04,381
I can just kill everyone.

207
00:08:04,381 --> 00:08:05,916
It's a catch-all equation.

208
00:08:05,916 --> 00:08:09,120
But, I still don't remember why
everyone's trying to kill me.

209
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:11,388
I just remember people
showing up and shooting.

210
00:08:11,388 --> 00:08:12,556
That's not very progressive.

211
00:08:12,556 --> 00:08:13,324
[lock buzzes]

212
00:08:13,324 --> 00:08:14,024
Are you kidding me?

213
00:08:14,024 --> 00:08:15,659
This is the fucking lobby!

214
00:08:15,659 --> 00:08:17,228
Why are these doors locked?

215
00:08:17,228 --> 00:08:18,562
From the inside!

216
00:08:18,562 --> 00:08:19,930
P.A.: Access Denied

217
00:08:19,930 --> 00:08:21,432
Who said that?!

218
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,335
Somebody's watching me.

219
00:08:25,970 --> 00:08:26,504
Fine!

220
00:08:26,504 --> 00:08:29,240
They don't want me to leave the
building, I can improvise.

221
00:08:30,774 --> 00:08:32,576
Watch the glass...

222
00:08:32,576 --> 00:08:35,779
I have a good suit but if those
shards got in my eye, oh man.

223
00:08:36,514 --> 00:08:37,214
Dammit.

224
00:08:38,149 --> 00:08:38,916
Come on!

225
00:08:39,617 --> 00:08:41,352
There's no grip.

226
00:08:41,352 --> 00:08:44,622
All right, I'm going to have to
go find a crate or something.

227
00:08:44,622 --> 00:08:45,990
Th-this is doable.

228
00:08:45,990 --> 00:08:50,060
Y'know, I seem to remember
having seen a crate before.

229
00:08:50,628 --> 00:08:51,996
Hm.

230
00:08:54,064 --> 00:08:55,633
Or a grappling hook!

231
00:08:55,633 --> 00:08:58,169
Wow, I could really
use a grappling hook.

232
00:08:58,169 --> 00:09:01,388
I'm going to buy one from Play It Again
Sports or someplace once I get out of here.

